cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Web Quality System — an open blueprint"
message: "If you use this system, or the vocabulary it defines, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Climent
    given-names: Manuel
    affiliation: Climent Media
    website: "https://climentmedia.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Manucliment/web-quality-system"
url: "https://climentmedia.com"
abstract: >-
  A complete method and gate suite for building, migrating, auditing and
  shipping static websites, distilled from real client work. Documents the
  measured finding that writing a rule down improves compliance by fifteen
  points and nothing more, and the consequence: a deploy door that refuses
  to open without a signed receipt naming the verdict per lens, the hash of
  the measured tree, the scope of the measurement, and the list of what
  nobody looked at. Includes the three-state verdict vocabulary that
  separates a pass from an unmeasured check, the expiring-acceptance
  mechanism that keeps a gate satisfiable, the served-equals-measured check,
  and a trap log in which forty-one of a hundred and ten documented defects
  belonged to the measuring instrument rather than to the sites.
keywords:
  - web-quality
  - static-sites
  - qa-automation
  - technical-seo
  - accessibility
  - web-performance
  - site-migration
  - deployment-gates
